# Slither's findings on contracts/src that are accepted, each with the
# reason. contracts/slither fails on a finding not listed here, and on an
# entry here that slither no longer reports. Before listing a finding, fix it
# if it is a defect; a defect under src/money/ or src/authority/ goes to the
# owner first (SEAMS.md).
#
# Each entry is the finding's key as contracts/slither prints it: the
# detector, then each line of slither's description, without file paths or
# line numbers, joined by " | ". That names the contract and function, the
# call or event, and the calling path where slither gives one. Then one
# indented line gives the reason. A finding slither reports twice under the
# same key is listed twice, or the second one fails the check.
# Slither 0.11.6, first run: 12 findings, all accepted below.

calls-loop: Claims._part(uint256,address,address,uint256) has external calls inside a loop: RewardMath.partOf(pot,ledger.bondAt(holder,node,round),ledger.stakeAt(node,round)) | Calls stack containing the loop: | Claims.withdrawParts(address,uint256[])
    The calls are views on StakeLedger, fixed at deployment; the loop is over the rounds the caller lists, so a long list costs only the caller.
calls-loop: Claims._part(uint256,address,address,uint256) has external calls inside a loop: RewardMath.partOf(pot,ledger.bondAt(holder,node,round),ledger.stakeAt(node,round)) | Calls stack containing the loop: | Claims.withdrawValidatorParts(address,uint256[])
    The calls are views on StakeLedger, fixed at deployment; the loop is over the rounds the caller lists, so a long list costs only the caller.
calls-loop: Claims._payMember(address,uint256,uint256,uint256,uint256) has external calls inside a loop: cut = RewardMath.cutOf(paid,ledger.cutAt(m,round)) | Calls stack containing the loop: | Claims.mintRoundShares(uint256)
    A view on StakeLedger, fixed at deployment, once per member of the round, at most Scores' N = 3.
calls-loop: Claims._payMember(address,uint256,uint256,uint256,uint256) has external calls inside a loop: lpt.mint(payout,cut) | Calls stack containing the loop: | Claims.mintRoundShares(uint256)
    TestLPT, fixed at deployment, mints without calling the recipient; once per member of the round, at most N = 3.
calls-loop: Claims._payMember(address,uint256,uint256,uint256,uint256) has external calls inside a loop: payout = registry.payoutOf(m) | Calls stack containing the loop: | Claims.mintRoundShares(uint256)
    A view on Registry, fixed at deployment, once per member of the round, at most N = 3.
calls-loop: Claims.mintRoundShares(uint256) has external calls inside a loop: stakes[i] = ledger.stakeAt(members[i],round)
    A view on StakeLedger, fixed at deployment, once per member of the round, at most N = 3.
calls-loop: Scores._seat(address,uint256) has external calls inside a loop: s = ledger.stakeAt(next[j],r) | Calls stack containing the loop: | Scores.optIn(address)
    A view on StakeLedger, fixed at deployment, over the N = 3 seats.
calls-loop: Scores._seat(address,uint256) has external calls inside a loop: s = ledger.stakeAt(next[j],r) | Calls stack containing the loop: | Scores.seat(address)
    A view on StakeLedger, fixed at deployment, over the N = 3 seats.
divide-before-multiply: Broker.redeemWinningTicket(ITicketBroker.Ticket,bytes,uint256) performs a multiplication on the result of a division: | - nodeAmount = paid / ONE * NODE_CUT + paid % ONE * NODE_CUT / ONE
    paid / ONE * NODE_CUT + paid % ONE * NODE_CUT / ONE is exactly floor(paid * NODE_CUT / ONE), since paid = (paid / ONE) * ONE + paid % ONE; it is split so no product overflows.
reentrancy-events: Reentrancy in StakeLedger.bond(address,uint256): | External calls: | - require(bool,string)(lpt.transferFrom(msg.sender,address(this),amount),transfer failed) | Event emitted after the call(s): | - Bonded(msg.sender,node,amount,now_ + 1)
    Every state change comes before the transfer, and the token is TestLPT, fixed at deployment, which calls no one; only the event follows it.
reentrancy-events: Reentrancy in StakeLedger.withdrawUnbonded(): | External calls: | - require(bool,string)(lpt.transfer(msg.sender,ready),transfer failed) | Event emitted after the call(s): | - UnbondedWithdrawn(msg.sender,ready)
    Every state change comes before the transfer, and the token is TestLPT, fixed at deployment, which calls no one; only the event follows it.
uninitialized-local: Scores.scoreOf(address).s is a local variable never initialized
    A memory array starts as zeros, and the insertion sort reads only the entries s[0..k) it has already written.
